# Public values only. Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the client bundle (web and
# APK) and readable by every user. Never put secrets here, in .env files, or in CI variables
# with this prefix: `node scripts/check-public-env.mjs` fails CI when a value looks like a secret.
#
# Copy to .env.local (ignored by git) for local overrides; nothing here is required to run.

# Base path when the web export is served under a subpath. GitHub Pages project site:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_BASE_URL=/BiblicAPP
# Leave unset for local development and for a site served at the domain root.

# Later milestones (not used in M0):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<publishable/anon key>   # public by design; never a service_role key
